    "#ScienceForKids"
  ],
  "tags": [
    "volcanoes for kids",
    "how volcanoes erupt",
    "magma and lava",
    "layers of the earth for kids",
    "ring of fire",
    "earth science for kids",
    "science for kids"
  ],
  "cast": [
    "LEO",
    "MIA"
  ],
  "loop_card": {
    "text": "How do volcanoes erupt?",
    "cue": "next",
    "left": "🌋",
    "right": "💥"
  },
  "lines": [
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Mia, how do volcanoes erupt? And where does all that lava come from?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "🌋",
          "label": "Volcano"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "💥",
          "label": "Erupt?"
        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Great questions! Let's dig deep into the Earth, find the melted rock, and watch it burst out of the top.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "⛏️",
        "text": "Dig deep!",
        "cue": "dig",
        "sub": "Find the melted rock",
        "sub_cue": "melted"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Dig? I'll get my shovel!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "We'll need a super long pretend shovel! The Earth is made of layers, a bit like a peach.",
      "chapter": "Inside the Earth",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:General_items/Servier/earth",
        "text": "Earth has layers",
        "cue": "layers",
        "sub": "A bit like a peach",
        "sub_cue": "peach"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "A peach? Yum!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "On the outside is the crust, thin like the peach skin. That's where we live. Below it is the mantle: thick, very hot rock.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Earth's layers",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🏡",
            "label": "Crust: where we live",
            "cue": "crust"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔥",
            "label": "Mantle: hot rock",
            "cue": "mantle"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And in the very middle?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "The core! It's like the peach's pit, and it's super, super hot.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🟠",
        "text": "The core: super hot!",
        "cue": "core",
        "sub": "Like the peach pit",
        "sub_cue": "pit"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So where does magma come from?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "In some places deep down, it's hot enough for rock to melt. Melted rock underground is called magma.",
      "punch": "magma",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔥",
        "text": "Melted rock",
        "cue": "melted",
        "sub": "Called magma!",
        "sub_cue": "magma"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How does the magma get out?",
      "chapter": "How it erupts"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Magma is lighter than the solid rock around it, so it slowly rises, like a bubble in honey.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🍯",
        "text": "Lighter, so it rises",
        "cue": "lighter",
        "sub": "Like a bubble in honey",
        "sub_cue": "bubble"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Then where does it go?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "It gathers in a big underground pocket called a magma chamber, under the volcano.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🕳️",
        "text": "Magma chamber",
        "cue": "chamber",
        "sub": "Under the volcano",
        "sub_cue": "volcano"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And then it just waits there?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Magma has gas mixed in, like the bubbles in a fizzy drink. The gas pushes harder and harder.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🥤",
        "text": "Gas bubbles inside",
        "cue": "gas",
        "sub": "Like a fizzy drink",
        "sub_cue": "fizzy"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Like a shaken-up bottle of fizzy water?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Exactly! When the push gets too strong, the magma bursts up through cracks and out of the top. Eruption!",
      "punch": "eruption",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "Eruption!",
        "traveler": "🔥",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "💨",
            "label": "Gas pushes",
            "cue": "push"
          },
          {
            "icon": "⬆️",
            "label": "Up the cracks",
            "cue": "cracks"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🌋",
            "label": "Out the top",
            "cue": "top"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💥",
            "label": "Eruption!",
            "cue": "eruption"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And then it's called lava!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Right! Magma is underground, lava is outside. Fresh lava is much hotter than an oven, and it glows red and orange.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "Underground",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "🔴",
              "text": "Magma",
              "cue": "magma"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Outside",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "🌋",
              "text": "Lava",
              "cue": "lava"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What else comes out?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Clouds of ash and gas, and sometimes chunks of rock! Volcano ash is made of tiny bits of rock.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "What comes out",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "☁️",
            "label": "Ash clouds",
            "cue": "ash"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💨",
            "label": "Gas",
            "cue": "gas"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🪨",
            "label": "Rocks",
            "cue": "rock"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Do all volcanoes look the same?",
      "chapter": "Kinds of volcanoes"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Nope! Some are tall and pointy, with steep sides. Their eruptions are often explosive.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "⛰️",
        "text": "Tall and steep",
        "cue": "tall",
        "sub": "Often explosive",
        "sub_cue": "explosive"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Boom!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Others are wide and gently sloping, like a shield lying on the ground. Their runny lava oozes out like a slow, glowing river.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🛡️",
        "text": "Shield volcanoes",
        "cue": "shield",
        "sub": "Runny lava flows",
        "sub_cue": "runny"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Is every volcano erupting all the time?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "No! Volcanoes that can still erupt are called active. Ones taking a long rest are dormant. And ones that are done for good are extinct.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Volcano moods",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🌋",
            "label": "Active: can erupt",
            "cue": "active"
          },
          {
            "icon": "😴",
            "label": "Dormant: resting",
            "cue": "dormant"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🏁",
            "label": "Extinct: all done",
            "cue": "extinct"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Where are most volcanoes?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Earth's crust is cracked into giant pieces called plates. Lots of volcanoes are where the plates meet.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🧩",
        "text": "Cracked into plates",
        "cue": "cracked",
        "sub": "Volcanoes where they meet",
        "sub_cue": "meet"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Like a giant puzzle!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! Around the Pacific Ocean there are so many volcanoes, it's nicknamed the Ring of Fire.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌊",
        "text": "Around the Pacific",
        "cue": "pacific",
        "sub": "The Ring of Fire!",
        "sub_cue": "ring"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Ring of Fire! That sounds like a superhero name!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Here's something amazing: volcanoes can build brand-new land!",
      "chapter": "Volcanoes make land",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🏝️",
        "text": "Brand-new land!",
        "cue": "land"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Brand-new land? How?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Some volcanoes start deep under the ocean. They erupt again and again. Lava cools into rock, layer on layer, until an island pokes out of the sea!",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "Making an island",
        "traveler": "🌋",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🌊",
            "label": "Under the sea",
            "cue": "ocean"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔁",
            "label": "Erupt again",
            "cue": "erupt"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🪨",
            "label": "Lava cools",
            "cue": "cools"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🧱",
            "label": "Layer on layer",
            "cue": "layer"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🏝️",
            "label": "Island!",
            "cue": "island"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So an island can be a giant pile of cooled lava?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! The islands of Hawaii were made by volcanoes, just like that.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🏝️",
        "text": "Hawaii: volcano islands",
        "cue": "hawaii"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Are volcanoes good for anything else?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! Volcano ash makes soil rich, so plants grow really well. And heat from deep underground can even make electricity.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Volcano gifts",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🌱",
            "label": "Rich soil",
            "cue": "soil"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🌽",
            "label": "Plants grow",
            "cue": "plants"
          },
          {
            "icon": "⚡",
            "label": "Power from heat",
            "cue": "heat"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Are there volcanoes anywhere else?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! The biggest volcano we know of is on Mars. It's called Olympus Mons, and it's much taller than any mountain on Earth.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔴",
        "text": "Biggest one: on Mars!",
        "cue": "biggest",
        "sub": "Olympus Mons",
        "sub_cue": "olympus"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Whoa! Volcanoes in space!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "And scientists called volcanologists keep a close eye on volcanoes, measuring shaking and gas, to help warn people early.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔭",
        "text": "Volcano scientists",
        "cue": "volcanologists",
        "sub": "They help warn people",
        "sub_cue": "warn"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Quiz time! Question one: what do we call melted rock while it's still underground? Think...",
      "chapter": "Quiz time",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "❓",
        "text": "Quiz time!",
        "cue": "quiz",
        "sub": "Underground melted rock?",
        "sub_cue": "underground"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Magma!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔥",
        "text": "Magma!",
        "cue": "magma"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! Question two: what pushes the magma up and out, like in a fizzy drink? Think...",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🥤",
        "text": "What pushes it out?",
        "cue": "pushes"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Gas!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "💨",
        "text": "Gas!",
        "cue": "gas"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Right! Last one: which planet has the biggest volcano we know of? Think...",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🪐",
        "text": "Biggest volcano?",
        "cue": "biggest"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Mars!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔴",
        "text": "Mars!",
        "cue": "mars"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Awesome! So: rock melts into magma, gas pushes it up, it bursts out as lava, and cooled lava builds new land.",
      "board": {
        "type": "summary",
        "rows": [
          {
            "icon": "🔥",
            "text": "Rock melts: magma",
            "cue": "melts"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💨",
            "text": "Gas pushes it up",
            "cue": "gas"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🌋",
            "text": "Out comes lava",
            "cue": "lava"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🏝️",
            "text": "Lava builds new land",
            "cue": "builds"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Volcanoes are hot, loud and amazing!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌋",
        "text": "Hot and amazing!",
        "cue": "amazing"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "They sure are! Ask a grown-up to subscribe to The Curio Kids Club for more wonders, and share this with a friend! And next time someone asks... how do volcanoes erupt?"
    }
  ]
}